       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Even with normal liver function, that dose risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure. A single 3,000 mg dose is also above the usual 1,000 mg maximum per dose.\n\nHere are some options that may be what you meant:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total). You may have meant 3,000 mg as the daily total.\n- **1,000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum).\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nIf you really do want 3,000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. Because of the risk, I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, and I'll enter it right away."
